    bench: add STCP vs TCP/TLS performance benchmark
    
    Add a unified benchmark suite for comparing AF_STCP against plain TCP
    and TLS 1.3 over TCP using the same echo workload.
    
    The benchmark supports:
    
        plain TCP
    
        TLS 1.3 over TCP
    
        AF_STCP with protocol 253
    
        configurable clients, payload size and duration
    
        throughput and operations-per-second reporting
    
        connection latency measurements
    
        RTT p50, p95 and p99 statistics
    
        client-side CPU usage reporting
    
        automated local comparison runs
    
        TLS test certificate generation
    
        STCP support through direct libc bind, connect and accept calls
    
    Fix Python compatibility with the custom AF_STCP socket family by
    passing sockaddr_in structures directly to the kernel and explicitly
    wrapping accepted STCP file descriptors with AF_STCP metadata.
    
    Also fix a benchmark start race where worker threads could observe an
    unset deadline, causing zero-duration TLS runs.
    
    Benchmark results with 4 clients, 256 KiB payloads and a 30-second run:
    
    TCP:
    
        TX: 617.53 MiB/s
    
        RX: 617.53 MiB/s
    
        RTT p50: 1.317 ms
    
        RTT p99: 3.779 ms
    
        CPU: 144.1%
    
    TLS 1.3:
    
        TX: 51.81 MiB/s
    
        RX: 51.81 MiB/s
    
        RTT p50: 18.446 ms
    
        RTT p99: 28.754 ms
    
        CPU: 189.5%
    
    STCP:
    
        TX: 143.46 MiB/s
    
        RX: 143.46 MiB/s
    
        RTT p50: 6.151 ms
    
        RTT p99: 13.458 ms
    
        CPU: 95.6%
    
    STCP completed the test without errors and achieved approximately:
    
        2.77x the TLS throughput
    
        2.77x the TLS operation rate
    
        66.7% lower median RTT than TLS
    
        53.2% lower p99 RTT than TLS
    
        49.6% lower client CPU usage than TLS

