        🚀 Major Milestone Reached: STCP + MQTT over LTE is now fully operational
    
             After a long series of development, debugging, refactoring, and
             optimization sessions, I’m happy to announce that the first complete
             end-to-end demonstration of STCP (Secure TCP) transporting MQTT traffic
             over LTE is now working successfully.
    
             What was achieved?
    
                  ✅ Custom STCP transport integrated into Zephyr MQTT library
    
                  ✅ MQTT CONNECT / CONNACK flow working correctly
    
                  ✅ End-to-end encrypted MQTT communication using STCP
    
                  ✅ ECDH key exchange and AES-256-GCM encrypted transport
    
                  ✅ Nordic nRF9151 LTE-M platform support
    
                  ✅ Zephyr RTOS integration
    
                  ✅ Rust-based cryptographic and protocol implementation
    
                  ✅ STCP proxy successfully bridging MQTT traffic
    
                  ✅ Stable connection lifecycle and transport management
    
                  ✅ FSM, API lifetime, mutex, and threading issues resolved
    
             What is the architechture?
    
                     MQTT Application
                             ↓
                     Zephyr MQTT Library
                             ↓
                     STCP MQTT Transport
                             ↓
                     STCP API Layer
                             ↓
                     Rust Crypto Engine
                             ↓
                     LTE Modem (nRF9151)
                             ↓
                     STCP Proxy
                             ↓
                     MQTT Broker
    
             The system now successfully:
    
                  * Establishes LTE connectivity
    
                  * Performs STCP handshake
    
                  * Negotiates encryption keys
    
                  * Switches to AES encrypted transport
    
                  * Establishes MQTT session
    
                  * Receives MQTT CONNACK
    
                  * Publishes and receives MQTT messages
    
                  * Maintains encrypted end-to-end communication
    
             Why this matters
    
                The goal of STCP has always been to provide a lightweight,
                high-performance secure transport layer suitable for embedded
                and constrained devices while remaining independent of tradi-
                tional TLS stacks.
    
                Seeing MQTT traffic successfully transported over STCP on a real
                LTE-connected embedded device is a significant validation of the
                architecture and years of work invested into the protocol.

